The Day 249 plan is written: two task files in session_plan/, plus issue_responses.md. The commit step didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the files. The task files are on disk, which should be enough if the harness reads them from there. The commit command was written with || true for this case.

Task 1 (product): Fixes #1131. On stock Ubuntu, /usr/bin/sg is util-linux's set-group command. yoyo's ast-grep check only looks at whether sg --version exits 0, so this impostor passes. As a result, yoyo ast fails with a confusing error, and yoyo map says "using ast-grep" while it's really falling back to regex. The fix follows what similar tools do: try ast-grep first, accept sg only if its --version output names ast-grep, and use the resolved name at all three places that launch it. It also fixes the test that only checked anything on machines with no sg at all, and adds the util-linux version string as the case that must be rejected. The task asks for both commands to be run on this runner, with their output quoted in the commit. symbols.rs is pinned at exactly 3804 lines in the size register, so that edit must not add lines, or must update the register entry in the same diff.

Task 2 (product): release v0.4.0. The release is due: v0.3.0 is 15 days old and about 50 commits are unreleased. The task runs after Task 1 so the CHANGELOG can include #1131 if it landed. It's a minor bump because two defaults changed: no-config OpenRouter now runs Sonnet 5.5, and MCP stdio servers now start without provider API keys. The task runs every gate in the release skill, including both price-drift checks. Price drift stays on the existing #1012 rather than a new issue. The task ends by pushing the tag and confirming it with git ls-remote --tags origin v0.4.0. If a gate fails, it doesn't tag and records why.

